.SH NAME
ktm-thread \- Threads without C: spawn and join (errors come back), Mutex, Cond, RwLock, Once, WaitGroup and go, Channel, each, and a pool.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
import thread;
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Threads without C: spawn and join (errors come back), Mutex, Cond, RwLock, Once, WaitGroup and go, Channel, each, and a pool.
.SH TYPES
.SS Channel
.EX
struct Channel<T> {
    Mutex m;
    Cond notEmpty;
    Cond notFull;
    Cond taken;
    T *buf;
    i64 cap;
    i64 head;
    i64 len;
    i64 sent;
    i64 received;
    bool unbuffered;
    bool closed;
};
.EE
.PP
A queue of T between threads, held by value: make one with thread.channel<T>(cap) and free it with free() (or declare it scoped) once no thread uses it; threads share it by pointer.
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
    scoped thread.Channel<i64> ch = thread.channel<i64>(16);
    // a producer: ch.send(v) ... ch.close();
    // a consumer: i64 v; while (ch.recv(&v)) { ... }
.EE
.RE
.PP
With cap items queued send() waits for a recv(); with none, recv() waits for a send(). cap 0 is unbuffered: send() returns once a recv() has taken the value.
.SS WaitGroup
.EX
struct WaitGroup {
    Mutex m;
    Cond c;
    i64 count;
    bool failed;
    Error err;
};
.EE
.PP
Waits for a group of threads: add(n) before starting them (go() does it for you), done() as each ends, wait() until all have. Works as declared, with no init and nothing to free; don't copy one that is in use.
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
    thread.WaitGroup wg;
    for (i64 i = 0; i < 4; i++) { thread.go(&work, &parts[i], &wg); }
    wg.wait();
.EE
.RE
.PP
wait() throws the first error a go() thread threw.
.SS Thread
.EX
struct Thread {
    ThreadRun *run;
};
.EE
.PP
A started thread: join() waits for it. A Thread is joined once; a zero Thread, or one already joined, joins as nothing.
.SS Mutex
.EX
struct Mutex {
    i32 state;
    libc.pthread_mutex_t m;
};
.EE
.PP
A lock one thread holds at a time:
.PP
